<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n81687" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιμάχ-ητος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span></span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fought about, fought for</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ταῖσι φυλαῖς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1404
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς πολλοῖς [ὕδωρ</span>]
				<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				7.84
			</span></i> ; [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πενία] ἥκιστα
			περιμάχητον</span> not <i>a thing one would fight for</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Smp.</u>
				3.9
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				521a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				678e
			</span></i> ; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυναστεία ὑπὸ πάντων ἐρωμένη καὶ π.
					γεγενημένη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					8.65
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				7.24
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				10.17
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ π. ἀγαθά</span>
			<i>such as are matters of contention, highly prized</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1169a21
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1271b8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1363a8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Epicur.
				<u>Sent. Vat.</u>
				45
			</span></i> : 
				Sup.
			 -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότατος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				9.40
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Lyc.</u>
				26
			</span></i> : in <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Th.</u>
				319
			</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλις π</span>., prob. with
			collat. sense of <i>fought around, surrounded by
		battle.</i></div>
